<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Violence costs Buffelsfontein day's output.</title>
<headline>Violence costs Buffelsfontein day's output.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Buffelsfontein Gold Mining Co Ltd said on Monday that violence last week cost it in total the equivalent of one day's production.</p>
<p>But Buffelsfontein managing director Sam Goodwin said that lost production would be recovered during October.</p>
<p>At least 24 mineworkers were killed in ethnic clashes at the mine, police said last Thursday.</p>
<p>Buffelsfontein, 160 km southwest of Johannesburg, is owned by Randgold &amp; Exploration Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Goodwin said that, while tension remained, mining operations were back to normal.</p>
<p>Buffelsfontein produced 1,782 kg of gold in the three months to end-June.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 2711 482-1003</p>
